{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n30 pytest modules re-run a `scripts/check_*.py` gate over the real tree (\"the repository is clean\"), grep the `Makefile` for its invocation, and in several modules do both; the script already runs in `make lint` (`Makefile:266-439`), which CI runs via `_build-and-test.yml:102`, so a lint-wired script has one owner. The twin fails a second time for the same defect and doubles suite time for zero signal. Three scripts (`check_adr_numbers`, `check_docs_index`, `check_verify_gate_parity`) run only as CI steps (docs-gates action `:22` and `:59`; `_build-and-test.yml:145-152`), so their pytest twin is currently their only portable owner. Table (3), the single-owner table over all 33 scripts with the per-module delete and keep sets, is itemised in this ticket's first comment, with the two exceptions stated below. Cites are on origin/main 083620b0.\n\n## Approach\n- Delete the 72 collected nodes named in table (3) as amended here (the \"real tree is clean\", \"make lint wires it\" and \"runs the real script as a subprocess\" twins) from their modules; the `--strict-markers` `repo_policy` mark on deleted tests goes with them. Fixture tests on synthetic input are kept (per-module keep counts are in the table).\n- Exception to table (3), row `check_mechanism_delta`: KEEP `tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py::test_the_committed_baseline_matches_the_live_tree` and `::test_the_committed_tree_assertions_consult_marker_admission`. They are not twins of `--check` (which tolerates stale rows); they encode the baseline-tidiness contract (`set(baseline) | admitted == live`) that the operator-approved same-change drain rule and bug amoeboid-amateur-guillemot (1768-5b6f-958a-43e9) rely on, and the source-level pin that keeps that test marker-aware after a revert. Only `test_check_passes_on_the_committed_tree` and `test_make_lint_runs_the_ratchet` are deleted from that module (2 nodes instead of 4).\n- Delete `tests/unit/test_config_gate_wiring_heldout.py` whole (6 wiring tests, 109 LOC).\n- Add `python scripts/check_adr_numbers.py` and `python scripts/check_docs_index.py --check` after `Makefile:439` (below the `check_verify_gate_parity.py` line S2 adds), so every lint-target script has `make lint` as its one owner.\n- Scripts that keep a non-lint owner lose only the twins the table names: `check_readme_quickstart` stays CI-owned (docs-gates `:70`, `test.yml:189`, `gerrit-verify.yaml:352`; it executes the quickstart); `check_build_env_locked` (`release.yml:184`), `check_commit_message_wrap` (pre-commit `:78-80`), `check_import_walk` (typecheck `:505`), `check_orphaned_load` (operator diagnostic, `docs/orphaned-processes.md`), `check_server_manifest` (`_build-and-test.yml` drift step) and `check_terraform_tree_currency` (`terraform-drift.yml:112`) keep their existing owner.\n- Extend `_WIRED_GATES` in `tests/unit/test_make_lint_hygiene_wiring.py:27-30` to the full list of lint-target scripts (the 25 `make lint` rows of table (3) + `check_adr_numbers`, `check_docs_index`, `check_verify_gate_parity`); the list stays explicit by that module's design (a CI-only script must not become a `make lint` obligation silently). Landing rule for `scripts/check_mcp_library_parity.py`, which the MCP epic's derivation story masonic-excusable-guppy deletes together with its `Makefile:298-310` line: if that story has landed, the entry is omitted (27 entries); if this story lands first, that story removes the entry when it deletes the script. The census module's two parametrized tests replace every deleted per-twin wiring test, so wiring has exactly one census.\n- `tests/scripts/test_check_config_reads_red_proof.py` is untouched. Remove the imports and constants each deletion leaves unused (ruff F401/F841 names them).\n- The `test_check_adr_numbers_heldout.py`, `test_check_config_ownership_heldout.py` and `test_check_config_reads_heldout.py` remainders stay as separate files here; the held-out epic (traitorous-official-sunbittern) merges them later.\n\n## Scope\nIn scope: the table (3) modules under `tests/unit/` and `tests/scripts/` (the spec counts 41 including the `_heldout`, `_lock_47e9` and `_red_proof` twins), `tests/unit/test_make_lint_hygiene_wiring.py`, `Makefile`. Out of scope: every `scripts/check_*.py` itself (no check script is edited, added, nor removed), every CI workflow file, `tests/scripts/test_check_config_reads_red_proof.py`, the two kept ratchet tests named above, and the `_heldout` merges.\n\n## Testing\n`pytest --collect-only -q <the table (3) modules>` before: 688 nodes; after: 616 (688 - 72) plus the new census nodes (2 parametrized tests x 28 scripts, or 27 under the landing rule); both counts recorded on this ticket. `make lint` exits 0 and its output lists `check_adr_numbers.py` and `check_docs_index.py --check`; `pytest tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py -q` still collects `test_the_committed_baseline_matches_the_live_tree` and `test_the_committed_tree_assertions_consult_marker_admission`; `make test` green.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] No test under `tests/` invokes a `scripts/check_*.py` `main()`/`check()` against `REPO_ROOT`: `git grep -nE 'REPO_ROOT' -- tests | grep -E 'chk\\.main|gate\\.check|\\.main\\(\\[\\]\\)'` returns only `tests/unit/test_make_lint_hygiene_wiring.py`.\n- [ ] Every `make lint` script appears in `_WIRED_GATES` and every `_WIRED_GATES` entry appears in `make -n lint` output; the census module's two parametrized tests pass over every listed script (`pytest tests/unit/test_make_lint_hygiene_wiring.py`).\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_config_gate_wiring_heldout.py` is gone (`git ls-files tests/unit/test_config_gate_wiring_heldout.py` prints nothing), and the two kept ratchet tests still collect (`pytest --collect-only -q tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py -k \"committed_baseline_matches or consult_marker_admission\"` lists 2 nodes).\n- [ ] Node counts reconcile: 688 before, 616 plus the census nodes after, from the two `pytest --collect-only -q` runs recorded on this ticket.\n- [ ] `make verify` green."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788814837097734187,"uuid":"654e465e-6568-4039-8b3a-67040ed92f10"}